(r/'validation/EXISTING_RHS_AUDIT.md').write_text('''# Existing RHS audit — PASS\n\nCompleted before creating the Phase 2 stage or modifying engine sources. The audited stable baseline is `stable_rigid_sphere_near_field_v0_20260916_101617`; source hashes and exact line anchors are in the adjacent JSON.\n\n1. `rigid::assemble` builds one bulk diagonal and sets its RHS to drag times background velocity plus optional imposed drive. Translation drag is 6πμa and rotational drag is 8πμa³. Therefore `R_bulk * U_bg` is already present.\n2. `FlowGradientSampler::query` computes half curl with grad[i,j]=∂u_i/∂x_j. For Ux=γz it yields Omega_y=+γ/2, matching Phase 1R n cross g. Rotation is also already on the RHS.\n3. Pair excess matrix/RHS terms are added after bulk. For the Phase 2 isolated particle, the LAMMPS neighbor pair list must be empty, so these terms vanish.\n4. The engine evaluates backgrounds at start, midpoint and endpoint, calls `rigid::solve`, and passes its solution to RigidStorage. This fix assigns positions, velocities and angular velocities. It adds no drag. `pair_style zero` supplies neighbor infrastructure and no hydrodynamic drive; no second time integrator is installed.\n5. No existing RHS double counting was found. A naive insertion of R_bulk*q_free plus the wall correction would create double counting. The authorized integration adds only R_wall_excess to the existing matrix and b_wall_shear to its existing RHS.\n\nThe analytic adapter supplies U=d*g and Omega=0.5*n cross g through the existing Background structure. It does not call the frozen-flow or gradient sampler. With no imposed force, the assembled system is (R_bulk+R_wall_excess)q=R_bulk*q_free+b_wall_shear. No solved velocity is replaced by a reference value.\n''')
